  "summary": "Independent cold review of the concise study for liturgy/roman-rite/1962/propers/temporal/01-first-sunday-of-advent (provider gemini; synthesis.tex, sections/10-concise-inventory.tex through sections/14-concise-apparatus.tex, generated/scriptural-date-location-page.tex, research/chronology-table.tex, research/chronology-annotations.tex, and research/production-review.md) passes with zero blocking findings. Reading the concise study alone before opening sections/01-09 recovered all three distinct whole-formulary interpretations and their concrete divergences across Luke 21:25-33 (Gregory's literal heralds and ironic 'fruit of the world is its ruin' balanced by Cyril's bodily incorruption and Bede/Augustine's renewal per imaginem, versus Ambrose's symbolic Marian 'light cloud' and Gentile 'all the trees' and interior in singulis), Psalm 84:8 & 13 (Bellarmine/Sicard/Gueranger's Marian virgin earth and Bernard's Christ-as-Fruit, versus Augustine's Old Latin suavitas ploughing confessed hearts and Schuster's Eucharistic pledge), Romans 13:11-14a (Chrysostom's stadium runners and glittering armour of light, Durandus's Incarnational exchange, and Augustine's Confessions VIII.12.29 with the 1962 omission of v. 14b), Psalm 24:1-4 (Bellarmine's earthly briers, Beleth/Schuster's Nativity longing, and Augustine's totus Christus plus Aquinas's precepts-vs-counsels ascent), and the altar prayers paired with Bernard's Middle Coming. Concrete Page-2 orientation-v3 lookup on generated/scriptural-date-location-page.tex and research/chronology-annotations.tex succeeded: (1) Gospel Luke 21:25-33 pairs directly to Narrated event 'Jesus teaches in Jerusalem about the coming of the Son of Man' (Date unresolved) and Composition 'The Gospel of St Luke' (Disputed: c. A.D. 70; Before Acts and the end of Paul's Roman imprisonment); (2) Introit Ps. 24:1-3, 4 (Vg.; Heb. 25) pairs Traditional attribution ('David's reign in the usual chronology; Hebron, then Jerusalem' -> c. 1055-1015 B.C. with Corbett's 30-50-year note), Historical setting (Occasion date unresolved), and Composition (Before c. 165 B.C.); (3) Alleluia Ps. 84:8 (Vg.; Heb. 85) and Epistle Rom. 13:11-14 pair cleanly to their Korahite (c. 740-536 B.C.) and Romans (Proposals span A.D. 57-58) composition dates with Vg./Heb. explained once (the shared projection omits composition place on Rom. 13:11-14, a shared-projection fact rather than a synthesis defect). Direct verification against the accepted expansive study (sections/01-09), research records, and primary witnesses in src/sources/ (Durandus VI.2-3, Beleth LV & LXIV, Rupert III.2, Gregory Hom. 1.1-6, Ambrose Exp. in Luc. X.37-45, Cyril Sermon CXXXIX, Bede VI, Augustine Enarr. in Ps. 84 & Sermo 185.1, Bellarmine on Pss. 24/84, Bernard Missus est Hom. 1 & In Adventu 2-5, Schuster I pp. 321-323, Gueranger I p. 137, Sicard V.2, and Aquinas Postilla Ps. 24) confirmed that all standing defects from iteration 0 (SYN-001's seven factual/chronological/attribution errors, SYN-002's Page-1 author bundling, and SYN-003's recurring semicolon-chained author stacks and overloaded sentences) are resolved without introducing new source-dependent claims or dropping qualifications, and advisories SYN-004 and SYN-005 are also cleared. Read-only mechanical validation (check-content-preflight --edition synthesis, check-proper-components --edition synthesis, document-types refresh --check, and _proper_study.py check --edition synthesis) passed cleanly. Meaningful limit: this is a source-level cold review; no PDF was compiled or visually inspected, so physical-page placement beyond source-level zref markers and component structure remains unverified until an optional print export is inspected. Verdict: PASS."
